; At precision 7 the balancing check reads the residual through
; amount_t::is_zero, which prints it with stream_out_mpq
; (src/amount.cc:1417-1425) and finds the exact remainder 0.00000005
; rendered as 0.0000001, a nonzero digit, so the transaction does not
; balance.  The semantic bisimulation (test/semantic/check_all.py)
; replays this journal, so an oracle that read a remainder of exactly
; half a unit as zero accepts what C++ rejects.

commodity XAU
    format 1.0000000 XAU

2024/01/01 half unit p7
    A    1.0000000 XAU
    B    -0.99999995 XAU

test bal -> 1
__ERROR__
While parsing file "$FILE", line 14:
While balancing transaction from "$FILE", lines 12-14:
> 2024/01/01 half unit p7
>     A    1.0000000 XAU
>     B    -0.99999995 XAU
Unbalanced remainder is:
       0.0000001 XAU
Amount to balance against:
       1.0000000 XAU
Error: Transaction does not balance
end test
